{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2cc216388f21872236ca2d6d035d8e60c3edd4d1422ecfa8ddbb25b6da83800d","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider seam and multi-provider support strategy","key_entities":["provider_factory","BedrockProvider","provider_provenance","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","first_class tier","best_effort tier","docs/llm-framework.md","docs/adr/0059","capabilities.py","bedrock_model.py"],"problem_keywords":["llm provider","bedrock","provider seam","support tiers","provenance","documentation","adr"],"propositions":["rebar's provider seam is pydantic-ai's provider_factory hook, not a rebar invention, with per-run session management and builder bodies in leaf modules.","The provider registry uses membership qualification (not prefix matching) against KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES, with strict guard order for configured providers and permissive fallback for inline model strings.","Native Bedrock support uses BedrockProvider with ambient AWS credentials, no rebar-managed keys, and inference-profile ids (not on-demand ids) as documented defaults.","Provider support has two tiers: first_class (Anthropic, Bedrock with native builders and full fidelity) and best_effort (gateway/local OpenAI-compatible with rewriting risk and no guarantees).","Verdict provenance is stamped as an additive unsigned sidecar object on every tier, recording provider, model (provider-qualified), endpoint hostname, tier, and four capabilities fields."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787393920805228001,"uuid":"e7da1496-23a9-444c-933f-65ded53782ae"}